{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPWrEwHkYYxpwcqt8XiP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`ard setup` now has read-only checks for main's ruleset, the App's permissions and the merge settings. I ran `go test` on `internal/setupcmd`, `internal/github`, `internal/merger` and `internal/prwatch`. All pass, and `go vet ./...` and gofmt are clean. `make lint test` timed out in the sandbox, so I did not complete the full `./internal/...` test run.\n\n- **Policy:** it is built into `internal/setupcmd/policy.go` and never read from repo content.\n  - **Ruleset row:** it passes when an active ruleset covering main requires a pull request and the only bypass actor is the ard App in `always` mode. Extra actors, a wrong mode or a missing App each show up in the drift message.\n  - **App permissions row:** it fails if the App has `workflows` or `administration`.\n  - **Merge row:** it fails when `allow_rebase_merge` is on while the `ARD_VERSIONING` repository variable is on.\n- **Output:** each drift row prints the fix, either the settings URL or a `gh api -X PATCH` command. A forbidden or not-found read gives a `manual` row with the command to look it up by hand.\n- **Apply step:** any non-green row now skips the label apply step. These checks never write anything.\n- **Reader methods:** `github.Reader` and the fake gain `ListRulesets`, `GetMergeSettings`, `GetApp` and `GetVariable`. That is three more than the issue named, because the merge settings, the App's permissions and the variable also need reading. The fake gets seeders for each.\n- **Tests:** I added tests for the policy, the four new reader methods against a stub HTTP server, and the fake's seeders.\n\nI did not extend the shared `clienttest` suite, since it runs against a live API. The new reads are covered by the stub-server tests instead.\n\nTwo things need a real token to settle: whether the App's own token can read ruleset bypass actors, and whether it can read repository variables. A forbidden response already becomes `manual`. The report is in `.ard/347/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1014,"cache_read_input_tokens":58276,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1014},"output_tokens":690,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d267aa3-2f49-43fb-a9d9-ee80cf01548b","uuid":"528d50d1-1644-4880-bd7d-53b88074b29b","timestamp":"2026-11-25T10:48:55.485Z","request_id":"req_011ChPWrEnckpKJw6AiS6M6n"}
